WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
The tidal Thames runs from
Teddington, through London,

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.790
to the sea.

3
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.510
Pollution here does not simply flow away:

4
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.290
it moves up and down with the tide.

5
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.450
Yet after a heavy shower, raw sewage can
pour into it from outfalls in the river

6
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.590
wall.

7
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.570
When dissolved oxygen
falls below 45 per cent,

8
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.610
fish can die.

9
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.170
So why would rain send
sewage into a river?

10
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.090
Litter washed off the streets?

11
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.170
Factories opening their drains?

12
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.630
In this mission, you'll trace the causes
and impacts of sewage pollution in the

13
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:34.570
Thames.

14
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.910
Then you'll judge which
fixes stop the pollution,

15
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.970
and which only clean up afterwards.

16
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: explain why heavy rain in
London can send raw sewage into the Thames.
